			"notes": "The fourth overhaul, inspired by HHA Blood and Void: arenas that take part in the fight, a dramatic way to every boss and a signature mechanic per boss.\n\n**Arenas**\n- Every arena has a flat core plus raised levels; **cover works by line of sight** (pillars, gates, standards, the titan …) with a golden rune and a \"covered\"/\"seen\" status line\n- Arenas change during the fight: Zeus' island breaks into floes, Hermes' gallery collapses, columns break, chains snap — always announced\n- Exact blueprints: every arena is repaired when a fight starts and restored after victory, abort, server stop or a crash\n\n**Boss mechanics**\n- Sub-targets with their own bars under the boss bar (Bia, Brontes' anvil, Kampe's chain locks …)\n- Hermes' messenger run with bells, Hekate's *Dark Hour* stealth phase, Brontes' hammer gets stuck after a clean miss, Zeus' grounding grip throws his lightning back, Hades' fetters with three ways out, Kronos' hourglass ray with pillar cover\n- Wardens: chain posts, Sisyphus' boulder, Ixion's fetter bars, Tantalus' sluices; wardens now get knocked out instead of dying and protect their arena core\n\n**World**\n- 35 new blocks in the *H&H World* tab: Olympus marble, storm marble with pulsing veins, Tartarus basalt, soul vein basalt with a heartbeat, ember basalt, bronze — with stairs, slabs and walls (stonecutter)\n- Themed bridges on Olympus and a closed palace approach in five sections, with a pulse that grows louder towards the boss; RPG goals and arrow follow the new ways\n- Richer islands, palace and Tartarus buildings; old worlds get the new Olympus automatically as you approach (`world_retrofit`)\n\n**Fixed**\n- Client crash in busy fights (e.g. Zeus with two players)\n\nFull list in the [changelog](https://github.com/vibec-studios/HHA/blob/new/CHANGELOG.md). For Minecraft 1.21.11 (Fabric); requires Fabric API and Fabric Language Kotlin."
		},
