			"notes": "The big one: Olympus, the RPG mode and a complete rework of how every boss looks, moves and sounds.\n\n**Bosses**\n- New effect system for every boss, warden and Olympus enemy: smooth shader effects (light trails, rifts, flames, water walls, runes), real floor blocks that fly and land, glowing ground cracks\n- Screen passes at key moments: shock ripple, heat haze, Hekate's lunar eclipse, Kronos' time stop and gravity lens\n- Staged cutscenes for intros, phase changes and defeats with a guided camera, all skippable\n- Music per phase with smooth crossfades and victory stingers; capes, beards, wings and chains swing with springs\n\n**RPG mode**\n- New **HHA RPG** button in the main menu: pick Heaven or Hell, open a lobby and play with friends via a six-letter code\n- Tunnel lobby: your group floats in the armor of its path through a tunnel of light and flies straight into the arrival cutscene, no loading screens\n- Plays like its own game: chapters with goals and a direction arrow, island scenes, act end, an ending with credits, own HUD, journal (J), pause menu, death screen and rests\n\n**Also new since 0.6.2**\n- Olympus as a world of islands above the clouds with the path to Zeus, Hekate, Brontes, Kratos and Bia, plus the Tartarus wardens\n- New weapon models, physically simulated chains on the Hells Mace\n- Bosses are tougher and hit harder\n\nFull list in the [changelog](https://github.com/vibec-studios/HHA/blob/new/CHANGELOG.md). For Minecraft 1.21.11 (Fabric); requires Fabric API and Fabric Language Kotlin."
		},
